FILE: assets/css/listScroller.css
FEATURE: list-scroller-verification
DATE: 2026-10-05

================================================================================
CHANGE 1 — list in normal flow, container width left to wrapperStyle, late items covered
================================================================================

OLD_SECTION
/*list parent container */
.vlistParentXContainer{
    /* overflow: hidden!important; */
    width: 100%!important;
    position: relative!important;
    overflow-x: scroll;
}

/*Style list parent */
.vlistParentX{
    display: flex!important;
    white-space: nowrap!important;
    position: absolute;
    padding: 0px!important;
    list-style: none!important;
}
.vlistParentX{
    flex-direction: row!important;
}

/*Style list */
.vlist{
    flex-shrink: 0!important;
}
/*  */

NEW_SECTION
/*list parent container: its width comes from config.wrapperStyle (width:100% by default) */
.vlistParentXContainer{
    /* overflow: hidden!important; */
    position: relative!important;
    overflow-x: scroll;
}

/*Style list parent: in normal flow, so the container takes the list's height */
.vlistParentX{
    display: flex!important;
    white-space: nowrap!important;
    position: relative;
    margin: 0!important;
    list-style: none!important;
}
.vlistParentX{
    flex-direction: row!important;
}

/*Style list: every item, including ones added after initialize() */
.vlist, .vlistParentX > *{
    flex-shrink: 0!important;
}
/*  */


REASON
width:100%!important on the container beat any config.wrapperStyle width (verified: wrapperStyle 'width:300px' gave 1185px); the default wrapperStyle already sets width:100% inline. position:absolute on the list collapsed the container to 0px height (verified). padding:0!important is replaced by the module's inline !important paddings, and margin:0!important strips a ul's default margins. '.vlistParentX > *' keeps items added after initialize() from shrinking. The datePicker's own rules (.vDateBoxTool .vDateRangeCon, position absolute in a 180px box) still outrank these, so the picker is unchanged (verified).
